Depends who you ask.  Before the Alpha Platform got axed, Microsoft was
developing Windows 2000 for the DEC platform.  It was a top secret program
in Microsoft, so of corse everybody in the universe knows about it.  Go to
ftp://dutlbcz.lr.tudelft.nl/alphant/, find files named ab5.zip or ab7.zip.
ab5.zip is Windows 2000 Workstation release RC2 (Newer).  ab7.zip is Windows
2000 Server release RC1 (Older).  You will want broadband to download them,
because they are 300-400 Megs.  To install, unzip them, burn all the files
to a cd, then put it in your Alpha and select "Install Windows NT from a
CD".  The OSs' are 444 day trials, so set your internal clock to 2012, when
you finish the install, set it back to 2002.  This will give you 10 years
plus 444 days.

Have fun,
Jeremy

