Alpha, then add the array once you've got a working system. NT likes a small
boot partition on the boot drive (1 to 2gb) and all the rest as data drives.
You might think of adding a RAID card, makes life a little easier in dealing
with multiple HD's.
Check all SCSI ID's on disks and CDRom to make sure that there are no
duplications.  The disk with OS should be 0, CDRom is typically 4, number the
rest as you see fit but make sure that there's no disk with 7 as it is usually
reserved for the SCSI adapter.

Good luck!

TomC

