Don't give up!

I am working here with an AS 1000A and a Mylex DAC960PU (Firmware rev
2.73), it runs linux 2.4.17 with the included DAC960 driver just fine.

Short installation instructions:
- Update the AS 1000A firmware to rev. 5.7 ([1]).

- Update the Mylex DAC 960 firmware to rev. 2.73 (firmware at [2], Loader
for Alpha at [3]).

- Configure the array with [4].

- Compile a kernel 2.4.17 with DAC960 support (for me the easiest way to
accomplish this was to install a debian system on a temporarily attached
external disk, compile a custom kernel and then move the system to the
array.

- If not already in place, create the /dev/rd/cXdY[pZ] device inodes with
[5].

- If you intend to boot off the array remember that you cannot use
'root=/dev/rd/cXdYpZ' in /etc/aboot.conf but must use
'root=[major][minor]' (eg. 'root=3001' for /dev/rd/c0d0p1 as root)
instead.

- Have fun.

[1] http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/as1000a.html
[2] http://www.mylex.com/support/productgd/matrix.html#old-dac
[3]
ftp://gatekeeper.research.compaq.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.1/utility/swxcrmgr/ra200fl.exe
[4] 
ftp://gatekeeper.research.compaq.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.1/utility/swxcrmgr/ra200rcu.exe
[5] http://www.dandelion.com/Linux/DAC960-Utilities.tar.gz

hth & Greets
  Michael Keller
