Jeremy:

If all else fails, write down the current settings and then delete it. Re-boot
the system and then manually enter the boot information.  I don't remember the
exact verbage, but it should be fairly obvious.

There's no easy to see what's on the disks with AlphaBios unless you have a
working OS.

If your system has SRM Console, you can switch over to it and then mount each
disk and view the contents.  You won't be able to do anything with it, but at
least you will be able to see what is on them.

Good luck!

TomC

