> Hi people.
> 
> I have an Alpha ES40, and I've installed Redhat 7.1 - but I can't seem
> to boot into Linux.
> 
> I get to the aboot prompt, and select the option that specifies the
> console to be ttyS0 (option 1.) It starts loading the OS and mounting
> the filesystems and it all looks great.
> 
> But it never seems to finish booting. Even if I enter interactive
> startup and choose to load no services, the console hangs after asking
> if it should load the last daemon (local). It's on the network, but I
> can't log in (telnet: Unable to connect to remote host: Connection
> refused)
> 
> The console doesn't accept any input. Nothing I type seems to have any
> effect. Why doesn't it give me a login prompt???
> 
> Thanks very much!!!
> 
> Tony :)

Just thought I'd pop back in and document the solution - in case
someone has a similar problem in the future.

The problem was that the wrong kind of getty was running on ttyS0
after the install. That's why I never got a prompt. I booted into
single user and changed the inittab to fix this (removed mgetty from
ttyS0, and put a mingetty on ttyS0 - mgetty is for modems)

The reason that I couldn't telnet or rsh into the machine either, was
