Eric:

All 500A's use AlphaBios by definition as the "A" series was intended for
Windoze NT.  They can easily be modified to boot to the SRM console and
with a few hardware modifications can be made to run OpenVMS and Tru64.
It's quite easy to find out which console is currently on your computer,
simply boot it up and somewhere in the AlphaBios setups (don't remember
exactly where) there is an option to "Boot to Unix OS", select it and power
cycle the computer.  It should boot to the SRM prompt which looks like
this:
>>>_
OpenVMS and Tru64 are much fussier about graphics cards and SCSI
controllers than NT ever was.  Unless you have a Miata GL with on-board
SCSI you will most probably have to change the SCSI controller and the
CDRom drive, and depending on what graphics card you have, it might need
replacing.  If it doesn't have the 2mb Cache module, you'll need one of
those too.
You should also flash the latest version of Firmware (7.2-1), it can be
downloaded free from Compaq, here's a link:
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/digitalpw.html

Good luck!

TomC


