I had that problem with a Multia.  I'm pretty sure the compact disc was 
bad.  Make sure that you're using a good disc (no scratches or dust, 
high quality) and CD-ROM (some cheap CD-ROM drives don't read cheap CD-R 
discs very well).

Also, are you sure that you've properly terminated the SCSI bus?  You 
can't just hope that everything works.  You have to do it right.  Every 
chain *must* be terminated at the end, preferably with an active 
terminator (just buy an LVD/SE terminator for $25 and save yourself some 
grief).  Don't use passive terminators.  Don't use long cables.  Use the 
shortest cable possible, and verify that it passes the SCSI-2/3/LVD 
standard(s).  This stuff is important.

If you still have problems, try contacting your vendor.  I hope you 
didn't buy this thing on e-bay.




