releases due to lack of hardware and lost interest.
http://www.openbsd.org

FreeBSD has had an Alpha port for some time, but it's probably not quite
on par with Linux or NetBSD yet.
http://www.freebsd.org

Digital^WCompaq offers licenses to OpenVMS and Dig^H^H^HTrue64 Unix for
a not that big sum for personnal use.
Hit http://www.compaq.com or http://www.google.com for those.

There's probably another couple of not quite so mainstream OSes
available too. I think plan9 runs on Alpha. But if you want to get some
work done, you probably want to stick with the above choices.

