Hi Maurice,

I've exactly the same running under RH7.1 (running without additional
software)
It's better to use SRM instead of ARC. (in ARC --> choose another
OS -->Digital Unix)
then:
boot dka600 -fl root=/dev/scd0 (where 6 in 600 is SCSI -id of cdrom)
the system will "crash" and gets in aboot>
Here, choose to boot from a predefined kernel. Choose to install linux in
TEXT mode.
Using diskdruide, set the following filesystems:
/boot (64 Mb)
swap (twice internal memory)
/ (rest of disk(s), /usr /var and other will be created here)

-paul-





