> http://www.linuxalpha.org/faq/aboot.html

> I think what you're looking for is BOOT_OSFLAGS under "Booting Linux".
> Also look about half-way down the page under "The aboot.conf 
> configuration file"

>  >>> set BOOT_OSFLAGS 0
>  >>> b

> will probably work (assuming you already have the boot device defined).

Not enough.  Type also at SRM promt 'set auto_action' and you will see
obvious choices.  This assumes that 'set bootdef_dev' was done
previously and correctly.  Type 'show bo*' to see what is really the
current status.

The problem is that there is no timeout and if you will do that
then getting back to SRM prompt when you need that can be sometimes,
ahem, "interesting".  If you can boot then 'shutdown -h now' should
end up with an SRM prompt.

In general it is a good idea to type in SRM 'help | more' and follow
up with requests for particular topics - like 'help boot'.  You may
learn a thing or two. :-)

  Michal


