The default X Server for RedHat 7.1 is version 4.0.3, which I have gathered
does not work with the Multia due to a bug in the way the frame buffer
works.  I have a Multia UDB which I have just got working by using the
older X Server, version 3.3.6, instead.  To get this working, you
have to install XFree86-TGA-3.3.6-38.alpha.rpm (I hope I got that
right, make sure that the symbolic link in /etc/X11 for X points
to /usr/X11R6/bin/XF86_TGA instead of /usr/X11R6/bin/XFree86, and
use XF86Config rather than XF86Config-4.

From my search, none of the 4.0.x X Servers work with the Multia.
I haven't tried 4.1.x servers since I would have to compile them
myself.

Larry



